Tommi Syrjanen writes:
> Klaus Kassner <Klaus.Kassner@physik.uni-magdeburg.de> writes:

> But it is more frequent than undiggable walls. The only reason why I
> sometimes get stuck in the late game because of an inconvenient
> boulder is when I have thrown away too many wands of striking as
> unnecessary baggage and then I have to backtrack several levels back
> to find the nearest one.

That is difficult when you're on the Astral Plane...
(It happened to me that a door to one of the three main areas was 
blocked by a boulder thrown by a giant.  Had it been a boulder remaining 
after the giant was dropped, the game might have become unwinnable.  Or 
I would have had to wait a zillion turns until another giant became 
created...  Since that event, I don't drop my pick-axe in the end game, 
just to become unburdened. However, I drop all wands of digging after 
the Plane of Earth.)

> By mid-game a wand of striking is almost useless as an attack wand so
> I use them almost exclusively for destroying boulders and drawbridges.

That's true.  Actually I mainly keep one wand of striking for the 
purpose of destroying boulders.

>> So I keep the pick-axe, which is one of the most useful items of
>>the game, IMHO.

> Yes, pickaxe is useful but it is too heavy to carry with you if you
> don't stash loot.

I do.  And then, a pick-axe in a blessed BoH has only a weight of 20, 2 
per cent of maximum carrying capacity.  Moreover, I am not extremely 
stringent about not becoming burdened.  It is not really a problem, when 
you wear speed boots.  Whenever I need to be fast enough to count single 
turns, I drop the bag.  This includes fighting Demogorgon or an arch or 
master lich, but not the wizard.  (When I take on the wizard, I usually 
just put my BoH into my sack.)

> If you want to carry one, you have to sacrifice your spare weapons,
> spare food, and the majority of holy water. 

Hardly.  One potion outside a bag weighs as much as a pick-axe inside. I 
just need to spare four potions or two potions and two food rations. 
Also, holy water is rarely essential.  If it is just for getting things 
uncursed, scrolls of remove curse are more useful and weigh less.  It is 
not really necessary for many items to be blessed.  You want your 
unicorn horn and your (especially two-handed) weapons blessed (and your 
BoH, of course), for the rest it is not that important.

